# Next.js App Router

## Defaults

- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only for interactivity, browser APIs, or hooks.
- Prefer the App Router (`app/`) over Pages Router for new work.
- Colocate `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx` with routes that need them.

## Data & Caching

- Fetch in Server Components or Route Handlers — not in `useEffect` for initial page data.
- Use `fetch` with explicit cache intent: `cache: 'force-cache' | 'no-store'` or `next: { revalidate }`.
- Mutate with Server Actions or Route Handlers; revalidate with `revalidatePath` / `revalidateTag`.

## Boundaries

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — client component fetching initial data
"use client";
useEffect(() => { fetch("/api/items").then(...) }, []);

// ✅ GOOD — server component
export default async function Page() {
  const items = await getItems();
  return <ItemList items={items} />;
}
```

- Keep secrets (`process.env` without `NEXT_PUBLIC_`) server-only.
- Never expose API keys in Client Components or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` unless intentionally public.

## Files

- `page.tsx` — UI for a route
- `layout.tsx` — shared chrome (keep lean)
- `route.ts` — HTTP handlers
- `actions.ts` — Server Actions (mark `"use server"`)
